WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:28.470
Marik Makes His Move  God Combo

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.530
Way to go, Jonouchi!

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:39.530
But why didn't you take his Great Moth?

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:42.640
Isn't that rare card more valuable?

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:45.420
That's why you're an amateur.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:49.820
I don't have Larvae Moth or Cocoon of Evolution.

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:54.200
So even if I get Great Moth, I can't use it.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.530
If you say so.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:02.070
I think you didn't want to take Haga's Great Moth because he's known for that card.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:04.370
That's not true!

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:07.310
This is good.

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:11.170
Jonouchi, you've become more like a duelist.

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:13.740
Yugi should stay on his toes.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:17.110
Maybe I am that good.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:22.040
I wonder how Yugi is doing.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.600
Let's go, Jonouchi.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:27.140
Keep it up and win the next duel!

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.020
Yeah!

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.700
Yugi, wait for me.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:36.660
I promise to become a true duelist and challenge you again.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:59.380
Too bad, but your friend Yugi Muto...

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:05.660
...the Pharaoh that I hate for cursing my family will soon die.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:07.500
Marik.

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:10.450
Are you sending the puppet?

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:15.240
Yes.  I will enter the puppet and fight the Pharaoh.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:17.880
And kill the Pharaoh.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:23.880
C'mon, move.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.950
Hey.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:33.150
He's been like this since yesterday.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.650
He's amazing.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:36.460
He won't move an inch.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.850
Maybe he's a doll.

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:41.360
Move!

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.660
I'm sorry!

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:48.770
Run!

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:54.340
What was that?

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:57.800
Run!

00:03:58.260 --> 00:03:59.650
Run to Yugi!

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:15.700
I know what you're fighting for in Battle City.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.400
To regain your memories.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:19.740
Right?

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:21.470
You knew?

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:29.640
At first, I didn't know why you'd want to enter a tournament where you could only win rare cards.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:34.860
But you were searching for something very important.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:40.590
It took me years to build the Millennium Puzzle.

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:56.400
It allowed me to meet someone special - you.

00:04:57.450 --> 00:05:01.300
I was a coward with no friends, but you gave me courage.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:04.750
And now, I have many friends.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:07.120
It's all thanks to you.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:08.560
That's not true.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:10.690
You did it on your own.

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:13.690
It's my turn to help you.

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:15.100
Let's fight together.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:18.020
Even if I'm not much help.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:20.430
That's not true, partner.

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:24.370
I can do my best because you're by my side.

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:27.000
Now and forever.

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:28.870
Yeah.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:42.560
Someone's coming.

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:52.930
Who are you?

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:55.930
We meet again, Yugi the vessel.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:57.140
Marik!

00:05:58.160 --> 00:05:59.740
You remember me.

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:04.940
Yes, I'm controlling this puppet.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:09.010
And this silent puppet is only a vessel.

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:10.110
Vessel?

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:11.970
Yes.

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:17.500
My Millennium Rod has buried this mime's soul deep inside his heart.

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:23.590
He's an empty vessel with no emotions.

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:32.360
Unforgivable!

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:38.160
You're using a Millennium Item to control people!

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.640
I won't forgive you, Marik!

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:44.050
This fight is 3,000 years in the making.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:48.360
If we're destined to duel, then I can't turn it down.

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:50.950
I accept this duel!

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:52.970
That's good.

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:55.420
You're the one I'm after.

00:06:55.800 --> 00:07:00.400
If I win this duel, this puppet will kill you.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:07.150
Even if you flee, this puppet will hunt you down until he kills you.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:11.570
Can you really defeat me?

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:13.270
Be careful.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:15.520
He has a God Card.

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:16.780
God Card?

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:20.420
In that case, I'll defeat a god!

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:28.660
I can see it.

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:35.460
A battle related to the Pharaoh from 3,000 years ago is about to begin in this city.

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:38.440
This future is unavoidable.

00:07:38.670 --> 00:07:42.740
Those who are guided by destiny will gather here.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:53.880
The Millennium Ring informs me that the Millennium Items will gather in this city.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:56.950
And one of them is here.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:01.250
He's coming.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:16.950
I let it escape.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:25.420
What's this picture?

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:31.200
Something I don't know about will occur in this city?

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:32.650
Interesting.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:35.930
Let me join in.

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:43.960
He's also part of the destiny created by the Millennium Items.

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:48.840
And Marik, you're coming too.

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:52.130
Move out of my way.

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:56.350
Are you willing to use your Millennium Rod on me?

00:08:56.600 --> 00:09:00.120
I can if it's for our family's future.

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:02.130
Even on you, sister.

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:09.330
Marik!

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:15.260
I should've stopped him then.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:23.140
When the sister and brother meet again, will it be on a battlefield?

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:25.950
I will win.

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:32.980
After I defeat you, I'll get the final card from Kaiba.

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:38.250
With the three God Cards, I will become the Pharaoh.

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:41.920
I will be freed from this 3,000-year curse.

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:46.480
That's when I'll rule everything!

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:58.240
To regain my lost memories, I cannot lose.

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:00.480
I will win this duel!

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:03.380
Here I go!

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:16.480
Here I go, Marik!

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:17.620
Duel!

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:37.740
I draw first.

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:38.510
Here I go!

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:41.070
I set a card!

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:47.870
I summon Humanoid Slime in attack position!

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:52.750
I end my turn!

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:58.250
Humanoid Slime in attack position?  It only has 800 attack points.

00:10:58.750 --> 00:10:59.840
My turn!

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:01.070
I draw a card!

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:05.350
He's inviting me to attack.

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:08.580
To catch me in his trap.

00:11:09.080 --> 00:11:12.050
So I'll play a trap for his trap.

00:11:12.300 --> 00:11:14.260
I set one card!

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:18.150
And I'll summon this!

00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:21.690
Gazelle the King of Mythical Beasts in attack position!

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:27.000
I end my turn!

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:30.690
You're not attacking?  You're so cautious.

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:33.500
Or a coward.

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:36.470
You'll never beat me that way.

00:11:36.770 --> 00:11:38.210
We'll see.

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:43.100
I hope you see the God Card Slifer before you die.

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:46.270
Stop talking and draw.

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:51.090
I summon Worm Drake.

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:58.190
Then I'll play a card from my hand.

00:11:58.740 --> 00:12:00.460
The spell card Polymerization!

00:12:11.110 --> 00:12:14.650
I summon the Fusion Monster Humanoid Worm Drake!

00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:17.600
2200 attack points!

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:21.940
He fused two monsters to raise its attack points.

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:27.910
A Fusion Monster has to wait one turn before it can attack.

00:12:27.910 --> 00:12:30.220
I'll use that to my advantage.

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:32.090
Are you sure?

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:38.000
You think my set card is a trap card.

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:40.100
But it's not a trap card.

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:41.200
What?

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:43.100
I'll show you.

00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:44.950
I flip over my set card!

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:46.980
The spell card Quick Attack!

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:48.780
That card is...

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:54.780
The Fusion Monster speeds up, allowing it to attack this turn.

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:59.020
I'm not afraid of your turn.

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:04.060
I'm the type who thinks of an attacking strategy for my next turn.

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:10.420
Unlike you, I'm not a cowardly duelist who's afraid of a single set card.

00:13:11.510 --> 00:13:12.510
Here I go!

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:14.540
Humanoid Worm Drake attacks!

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:17.300
Destroy Gazelle the King of Mythical Beasts!

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:21.580
I flip over my set card!

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:30.780
What?  De-Fusion?

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:39.010
Marik, I knew that your first monster Humanoid Slime could be used to Fusion Summon.

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:41.050
You knew I would fuse?

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:48.800
Because Fusion Summoning is quicker than Tribute Summoning to bring out strong monsters.

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:53.150
Marik, plan your next strategy.

00:13:53.150 --> 00:13:55.110
And I'll solve that too.

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:58.150
This is fun, Yugi.

00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:02.320
Your strategy is too weak to erase my life points!

00:14:03.340 --> 00:14:09.110
I simply threw a pebble in the water this turn to see how far the ripples reach.

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:12.490
I was testing your dueling capacity.

00:14:12.770 --> 00:14:15.000
You couldn't even create a tiny wave.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:20.800
For a duelist, strategies are like water in a vessel.

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:25.010
The water changes shape depending on the vessel.

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:28.220
If the vessel is shallow, you can see its bottom.

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:34.820
As rumored, you're a duelist with a large and deep vessel.

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:41.300
But when I throw my boulder into the water, I'll destroy your vessel into pieces.

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:45.910
A godlike boulder known as Slifer the Sky Dragon!

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:49.600
Here I go!  It's my turn!

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:55.900
OK.  I'll summon a monster this turn and destroy his monster.

00:14:55.900 --> 00:14:59.510
Then I'll Tribute Summon Buster Blader next turn.

00:14:59.510 --> 00:15:02.350
I summon Beta The Magnet Warrior!

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:05.140
Battle Phase!

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:08.680
Beta The Magnet Warrior attacks Worm Drake!

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:17.330
And Gazelle the King of Mythical Beasts attacks Humanoid Slime!

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:28.170
Worm Drake and Humanoid Slime are destroyed!

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:33.600
Good.  Those attacks eliminated all his monsters.

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:36.910
I have the upper hand in this duel.

00:15:37.730 --> 00:15:39.730
You don't get it.

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:42.570
You're the one who's been cornered.

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:44.660
My turn!  I draw!

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:49.480
I compared strategies to water.

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:52.660
I'll now show you the ultimate strategy.

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:58.660
Water can transform into a shapeless shield that parries any attack.

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:02.840
It can also transform into a sword that pierces the enemy.

00:16:03.300 --> 00:16:05.840
This monster has those powers.

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:12.250
I summon Revival Jam in defense position!

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:14.430
Revival Jam?

00:16:14.430 --> 00:16:17.600
And I play another card!

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:31.160
I activate Jam Breeding Machine!

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:39.510
This machine creates a Slime Token with 500 attack points every turn.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:46.010
But if I summon a non-Slime monster, Jam Breeding Machine is destroyed.

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:47.950
I see, Marik!

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:53.950
You want to create many Slimes so that you can Tribute them to summon high Level monsters.

00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:55.000
Yes.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:17:01.960
I need to Tribute three monsters to summon the God Card, Slifer the Sky Dragon.

00:17:02.260 --> 00:17:04.080
Slifer the Sky Dragon.

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:07.470
The ultimate monster with unknown abilities.

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:12.480
Does he already have that card in his hand?

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:20.520
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:23.880
Buster Blader...

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:30.090
I must drop his life points to 0 before he summons Slifer.

00:17:30.560 --> 00:17:33.690
I Tribute two Level 4 monsters!

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:38.430
I summon the dragonslayer Buster Blader!

00:17:46.700 --> 00:17:48.600
Buster Blader!

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:55.360
You Tribute Summoned Bluster Blader, the legendary swordsman who slays dragons.

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:58.920
Go!  Attack Revival Jam!

00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:00.770
Destruction Sword!

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:05.320
Revival Jam is destroyed!

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:07.230
Look closely.

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:16.940
What?

00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:22.160
Are you surprised?

00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:25.510
This is Revival Jam's regenerative power.

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:31.950
Like how water has no form, it can regenerate itself even if it's destroyed and return to the field.

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:33.750
Regenerative power?

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:37.780
I told you that it's a shapeless, invincible shield.

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:42.760
As long as it's on the field, your monsters' attacks can't reach me.

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:46.670
It can regenerate even if I destroy it?

00:18:46.670 --> 00:18:50.400
This means I can never lower his life points to 0!

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:53.160
It's too late to do anything.

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:57.360
My special combo to summon a God is complete.

00:18:57.730 --> 00:18:59.860
You only have...

00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:01.800
...three turns left.

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:04.030
My turn.

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:06.760
Jam Breeding Machine activates!

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:11.390
It creates one Slime Token!

00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:14.100
And I set one card.

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:15.960
I end my turn.

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:21.500
What are you going to do, Yugi?

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:25.020
You'll create a Slime Token every turn.

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:32.080
When you have three, you're planning to Tribute them to summon the God Card, Slifer the Sky Dragon.

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:34.970
But your strategy isn't good enough!

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:39.920
My Buster Blader has 2600 attack points.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:44.090
Your Slime Token only has 500!

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:51.070
When Buster Blader destroys Slime Token, you'll lose 2100 life points.

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:55.770
You said I have three turns left, but you only have two!

00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:56.830
Here I go!

00:19:56.960 --> 00:20:00.170
Buster Blader attacks Slime Token!

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:02.510
I flip over my set card.

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:06.420
I activate the Continuous Trap, Jam Defender!

00:20:15.470 --> 00:20:18.660
What?  Revival Jam took the attack instead!

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:25.640
Jam Defender lets Revival Jam take any of your attacks instead.

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:28.900
Did you think I'd be unprepared, Yugi?

00:20:32.670 --> 00:20:39.010
I knew you could greatly damage my life points if you attacked my Slime Tokens.

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:46.850
It's my turn.

00:20:52.240 --> 00:20:53.830
A second Slime...

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:57.580
God will arrive on my next turn.

00:20:58.500 --> 00:21:03.710
I'll prepare a special seat for you with this card.

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:07.230
The spell card Nightmare's Steelcage!

00:21:24.330 --> 00:21:25.390
What's this?

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:44.080
Trapped inside Nightmare's Steelcage, Yugi can't attack.

00:21:44.080 --> 00:21:48.870
Meanwhile, Marik steadily prepares to summon his God Card.

00:21:49.150 --> 00:21:52.500
With thunder and a powerful flash in the skies...

00:21:52.500 --> 00:21:56.920
...the God Card finally shows itself!  Slifer the Sky Dragon!

00:21:57.070 --> 00:22:01.320
Yugi, is there any way to destroy this tremendous monster?

00:22:02.100 --> 00:22:04.630
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Slifer the Sky Dragon

00:22:04.630 --> 00:22:06.080
Duel, standby!

00:22:20.960 --> 00:22:25.470
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:26.260 --> 00:22:30.840
I feel like I've been here

00:22:31.360 --> 00:22:40.490
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:40.800 --> 00:22:52.000
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:54.890 --> 00:22:59.500
Time passes bit by bit

00:23:00.190 --> 00:23:04.800
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:05.360 --> 00:23:09.910
Will never change

00:23:10.570 --> 00:23:15.180
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:15.810 --> 00:23:20.390
To be who I am

00:23:20.980 --> 00:23:25.630
I've kept searching for something

00:23:26.280 --> 00:23:30.330
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:30.330 --> 00:23:33.270
I learned that's the answer

00:23:34.060 --> 00:23:40.370
From now until forever...
